{% doc %}
  Detects event-ticket products powered by the GM Event Ticketing app.
  Outputs "true" when the product is an event; empty otherwise. Callers
  capture the output with `{% capture %}` and guard product-specific
  metafields behind an `{% if %}`.

  Convention: event products carry `product.type` "Event" or "Ticket"
  (case-insensitive). The merchant sets this when creating the product
  in the Shopify admin via the GM Event Ticketing app.

  @param {product} product - The product to check. Required.

  @example
  {%- capture is_event_product -%}{%- render '_is-event-product', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if is_event_product != 'true' -%}
    ... product-only metafields ...
  {%- endif -%}
{% enddoc %}

{% liquid
  assign t = product.type | downcase
  if t == 'event' or t == 'ticket'
    echo 'true'
  endif
%}
